        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "Pino directly accesses `process.hrtime.bigint()` as a global (not through a module import). In the CF Workers runtime, `process` is the polyfilled process object from nodejs_compat. This polyfill doesn't include `hrtime`.\n\nThe issue: `process.hrtime` is `undefined` in the CF Workers runtime.\n\nThe fix: Either:\n1. Inject a global `process.hrtime` polyfill at the start of the bundle\n2. Alias `pino` to a CF-compatible logger\n3. Mark `pino` as external\n\nBut pino is deeply embedded throughout the server code. The easiest fix is to inject a `process.hrtime` polyfill into the bundle.\n\n\nI can add a banner to the esbuild config that injects a polyfill for `process.hrtime` at the very top of the bundle, before any modules initialize. This checks if `process` exists and `hrtime` is missing, then defines both the function and the `bigint` method to return a timestamp in nanoseconds.",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
